<AtTheTable>
Before considering a call, identify the current street, the amount already paid this round, and the amount to match. Before considering a check, make sure you face no unmatched wager. The frequency of pocket pairs tells you how often a starting shape occurs; it does not tell you whether a particular bet is worth calling.

You may skip this introductory chapter from the course page if the rules are familiar. You can open Chapter 1 directly; reading ahead does not award quiz credit.

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>
  A trading decision also starts with a clear description of the available
  actions and the cash already committed. Mixing a past payment with the cost of
  the next action can distort a comparison. Later, expected value will turn
  those action descriptions into weighted outcome calculations.
</QuantCorner>
